; bal -V --unrealized books no unrealized gain on an amount with no
; commodity.  The -1000 in Assets:Checking has no commodity and a cost of
; -200 GBP; the report cannot value it, so it contributes itself to the
; baseline and adds nothing to the unrealized rows, while the AAPL lot is
; revalued as usual.  Booking it at its cost instead printed an
; Equity:Unrealized Gains row of "1000 / $-200 / -200 GBP", which made the
; report total zero only by setting the pounds against the amount that paid
; for them.
; Under --dc the amount stays in the credit column and the one unrealized
; row is again the AAPL revaluation.

2024/01/01 Buy pounds
    Assets:GBP              200 GBP
    Assets:Checking       -1000 @ 0.2 GBP

2024/02/01 Buy shares
    Assets:Brokerage        10 AAPL @ $150
    Assets:Cash

P 2024/03/01 AAPL $170

test bal -V --unrealized --now 2024/04/01
               -1000
                $200
             200 GBP  Assets
               $1700    Brokerage
              $-1500    Cash
               -1000    Checking
             200 GBP    GBP
               $-200  Equity:Unrealized Gains
--------------------
               -1000
             200 GBP
end test

test bal -V --unrealized --dc --now 2024/04/01
         $1700
       200 GBP           1000
                      $1500          -1000
                                    $200
                                 200 GBP  Assets
         $1700              0          $1700    Brokerage
             0          $1500         $-1500    Cash
             0           1000          -1000    Checking
       200 GBP              0        200 GBP    GBP
          $200              0          $-200  Equity:Unrealized Gains
-------------- -------------- --------------
         $1500
       200 GBP           1000
                      $1500          -1000
                                 200 GBP
end test
